    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc7vEdDY",
      "title": "system-config: remove batchInbox and startBlock",
      "author": "mds1",
      "number": 922,
      "body": "Removes `batchInbox` and `startBlock` from the SystemConfig spec, matching https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/pull/21641 which removes the getters and clears their legacy storage slots at op-contracts v8.0.0 (SystemConfig 4.0.0).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. Removed the `batchInbox` and `startBlock` getter sections and their TOC entries from `system-config.md`.\n2. `initialize` MUSTs no longer include setting the batch inbox or start block; they now require clearing the two legacy slots.\n3. `configurability.md`'s Batch Inbox address section no longer links to the SystemConfig source, and notes the value lives in the rollup configuration only.\n\nWhy: during U19, OPCMv2's reinit path rotated the onchain batch inbox for pre-OPCM chains (ethereum-optimism/optimism#21614). Nothing in the OP Stack reads these values from the SystemConfig — the rollup config and superchain registry are the source of truth — so we're removing the redundant onchain copy rather than maintaining it.\n\nRelated PRs: https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/pull/21641 (contracts), https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops/pull/1492 (upgrade tooling), the dev-docs edit rides along in the monorepo PR.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-08T00:56:11Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-07-30T22:05:45Z",
      "additions": 34,
      "deletions": 19
    },
